From: FPGAmixer project
Subject: [PATCH] msg: ignore octets after messageLength

msg_post_recv() parsed TLVs over everything received and then required
the header plus TLVs to equal messageLength. macOS's gPTP (seen with an
OWC Thunderbolt Ethernet adapter, 2026-09-30) sends Follow_Up with
messageLength 96 (the 802.1AS Follow_Up information TLV and a 16-byte
Apple organization TLV) followed by a further 54-byte Apple organization
TLV outside the message. ptp4l parsed that too, found 150 bytes where the
message says 96, and logged "bad message" for every Follow_Up, so the
port never left UNCALIBRATED. Octets beyond messageLength are not part of
the message (as with Ethernet padding); ignore them.

FPGAmixer docs/phase10_status_2026-09-29.md sec. 10.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/msg.c
+++ b/msg.c
@@ -352,6 +352,15 @@
 	if (err)
 		return err;

+	/*
+	 * Octets after the message's own length are not part of it (e.g.
+	 * Ethernet padding). macOS's gPTP appends an Apple organization
+	 * TLV after messageLength on Follow_Up; parsing it made every
+	 * Follow_Up a "bad message".
+	 */
+	if (cnt > m->header.messageLength)
+		cnt = m->header.messageLength;
+
 	type = msg_type(m);

 	switch (type) {
